      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is safe because if N were `a+b` it would be a non-trivial expression so then `writeNontrivialScratchLet` would store it in a temporary and then `N` would just be the variable reference.\n\n`writeNonTrivialScratchLet` is going away in https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1118697, so I will double-check how this situation behaves in that CL and see if the precedence should be switched.",
